    "steps": [
      "Salt the eggplant slices, leave for 20 minutes, then pat dry. Brush with oil and roast at 220 C for about 20 minutes, turning once, until golden. (Frying works too.)",
      "For the meat sauce, soften the onion in a little oil for 6 minutes, add the garlic and the beef and brown, breaking up lumps.",
      "Add the tomato paste, wine, tomatoes, cinnamon, allspice and bay and simmer for 25 minutes until thick. Stir in the parsley and season.",
      "For the béchamel, melt the butter, stir in the flour for 2 minutes, then whisk in the milk gradually and cook until thick. Season with salt and nutmeg, cool a little, then beat in the eggs and half the cheese.",
      "Heat the oven to 180 C. In a deep 30 x 20 cm dish, layer half the eggplant, all the meat sauce, then the remaining eggplant. Spread over the béchamel and top with the rest of the cheese.",
      "Bake for 45 minutes until deep golden. Rest for 20 minutes before cutting so the layers hold."
    ],
    "notes": "Lamb or a mix of lamb and beef is also common. Thin sliced fried potatoes are layered in some regional versions.",
